# SWISH -- family: MOVEMENT.
# Idea: a drum has no LFO, so these macros shape how the hit moves through
# time instead of its tone:
#   OPEN   the pedal: a tight "tss" with a hard tick .. a long wash whose
#          attack softens as it opens
#   ECHO   the hit repeats in time: the delay send opens and the hat gets a
#          little darker and shorter, so the repeats carry the rhythm
#   SHIMR  the tail blooms: more resonance (a ringing band) and more reverb,
#          so the hit swells after it lands
# Feel if it works: the open hat breathes with the groove; OPEN + ECHO on the
# pad turns one off-beat hat into a rhythmic pattern.
# Try: OPEN on X, ECHO on Y with off-beat open hats.
voice ohh
name SWISH
about "Open the pedal, let echoes ride."
base tone=72 mtl=84 tune=64 sprd=64

macro OPEN 0.4
  dcy      0:14 0.4:52 1:118
  snap     0:66 0.4:32 1:6
  colr     0:44 1:66
  lvl      0:100 0.4:94 1:88         # a long wash builds up: hold it down

macro ECHO
  dly      0:10 0.2:40 1:112
  tone     add 0:0 1:-18
  dcy      add 0:0 1:-22             # shorter hits, clearer repeats
  lvl      add 0:0 1:-4

macro SHIMR
  colr     add 0:0 1:52
  rev      0:24 1:110
  dcy      add 0:0 1:16
  lvl      add 0:0 1:-4
